<http://data.silknow.org/event/4bbea54c-4705-37f3-85a9-0699b95f0d82>
        a                              ecrm:E8_Acquisition ;
        rdfs:comment                   "Acquired in 1864 as part of the collection of Dr. Franz Bock.\n\nHistorical significance: A very well-preserved example of 14th century Italian velvet, illustrating a pomegranate motif, a key feature of luxury textile design of this period, as well as the use of polychrome silks and gold thread."@en ;
